#: ../../../news.rst:11
msgid "Current release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:14
msgid "Psycopg 3.3.9"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:16
msgid ""
"Use the C implementation of the wait functions on Windows too. It was "
"disabled because of an excessive CPU usage, fixed in Psycopg 3.2.11 "
"(:ticket:`#645`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:19
msgid ""
"Fix binary dumping of `!Int4Range` and other typed ranges and multiranges "
"(:ticket:`#1157`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:21
msgid "Fix dumping of Decimal 0 with large exponent (part of :ticket:`#1414`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:22
msgid ""
"Close the connection if the query cancellation following a Ctrl-C or a task "
"cancellation is interrupted again, instead of leaving it stuck in ACTIVE "
"state (:ticket:`#1435`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:25
msgid ""
"Limit the memory used by :sql:`COPY FROM` if the server consumes data slower "
"than it is produced. Add a `!flush_threshold` parameter to "
"`~copy.LibpqWriter` to tune it (:ticket:`#1437`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:28
msgid ""
"Don't wait on the event loop when the socket is already writable, which made "
"pipeline mode, `~AsyncCursor.executemany()` and `~AsyncCopy.write()` on "
"async connections several times slower than on sync ones (:ticket:`#1468`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:32
msgid ""
"Fix client-side quoting of negative zero floats and decimals, which could "
"produce a ``--`` SQL comment (:ticket:`#1480`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:34
msgid ""
"Raise `DataError` instead of `!ValueError` registering a composite whose "
"name or attributes are not valid namedtuple names, for instance Python "
"keywords (:ticket:`#1482`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:37
msgid ""
"Speed up the C implementation of the sync wait function, in particular when "
"the connection doesn't need to wait, for instance at every `~Copy.write()` "
"(:ticket:`#1484`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:40
msgid ""
"Don't replace the exception raised in a :sql:`COPY` block, for instance an "
"interruption, with an error terminating the operation (:ticket:`#1486`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:42
msgid ""
"Fix `~copy.QueuedLibpqWriter` hanging forever, instead of raising the error, "
"if sending data to the server fails while its queue is full "
"(:ticket:`#1489`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:45
msgid "Performance improvements to lists dumping (:tickets:`#1490, #1491`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:46
msgid "2.5x faster UUID loading in the C implementation (:ticket:`#1494`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:47
msgid ""
"Reduce the size of the binary packages by about 15 to 40%, depending on the "
"platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:52
msgid "Psycopg 3.3.8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:54
msgid ""
"Revert the use of ``/etc/ssl`` as SSL directory in the binary packages on "
"Linux and macOS: it caused the system ``openssl.cnf`` to be loaded, which "
"could break connections, for instance on FIPS-enabled systems "
"(:ticket:`#1476`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:58
msgid ""
"Fix the size of the binary packages on Linux x86_64, increased in 3.3.7 by "
"padding of the bundled libraries (:ticket:`#1477`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:63
msgid "Psycopg 3.3.7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:65
msgid ""
"Fix segfault fetching arrays of strings or timestamps after closing the "
"connection (:ticket:`#1428`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:67
msgid ""
"Fix `~Connection.cancel_safe()` failing if the cancel connection is not "
"ready immediately, for instance on a slow network (:ticket:`#1440`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:69
msgid ""
"Fix reference cycles created adapting recursive types, which kept data in "
"memory until the next garbage collection (:tickets:`#1443, #1462`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:71
msgid ""
"Fix loading intervals with a very large number of hours in text format, "
"which could lose microseconds (:ticket:`#1446`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:73
msgid ""
"Fix leak of adapters calling `~psycopg.types.composite.register_composite()` "
"repeatedly without custom `!make_object` or `!make_sequence` functions "
"(:ticket:`#1449`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:76
msgid ""
"Roll back the transaction if entering a `~Connection.transaction()` block is "
"interrupted, for instance by a task cancellation (:ticket:`#1451`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:78
msgid ""
"Quote array elements with Unicode white space, which CockroachDB would "
"otherwise strip from strings (`cockroach#176211`__, :ticket:`#1465`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:80
msgid ""
"Set the system SSL root certificate directory to ``/etc/ssl`` in the binary "
"packages on Linux and macOS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:87
msgid "Psycopg 3.3.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:89
msgid "Add support for Python 3.15 (:ticket:`#1245`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:90
msgid ""
"Improve performance of async queries by reducing the overhead of the `!"
"wait_async()` function (:ticket:`#1331`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:92
msgid ""
"Don't wait forever for a query to terminate after interrupting it, for "
"instance if the server is unresponsive. The fix requires libpq 17 or newer "
"(:ticket:`#1371`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:95
msgid "Cancel a running query upon receiving `!SystemExit` (:ticket:`#1384`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:96
msgid ""
"Report `!None` instead of ``65535`` as the `Column.precision` of "
"an :sql:`interval` column declared with a fields restriction and no explicit "
"precision, such as e.g. :sql:`interval day to second` (:ticket:`#1397`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:99
msgid "Fix dumping of nested subclasses of lists as arrays (:ticket:`#1398`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:100
msgid ""
"Discard prepared statements upon :sql:`DEALLOCATE ALL` (:ticket:`#1408`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:101
msgid ""
"Better guards dumping large Python `!int` to binary numeric "
"(:ticket:`#1414`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:105
msgid "Psycopg 3.3.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:107
msgid ""
"Discard prepared statements upon :sql:`ALTER *` or `DISCARD *` "
"(:ticket:`#1307`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:109
msgid ""
"Fix `!ProgrammingError` when dumping non-`!None` values with no `!NoneType` "
"dumper registered in python implementation (:ticket:`#1325`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:111
msgid ""
"Fix `!wait_selector` wait function to not raise `!KeyError` "
"(:ticket:`#1327`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:113
msgid ""
"Fix `!DataError` messages leaking the literal ``{...}`` placeholder instead "
"of the offending value when loading a pre-year-1 :sql:`timestamp` or a "
"malformed binary :sql:`jsonb` value (:ticket:`#1372`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:116
msgid ""
"Raise `!DataError` instead of `!ValueError` when "
"`~psycopg.rows.namedtuple_row` receives duplicate column names "
"(:ticket:`#1348`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:118
msgid "Raise `!DataError` on inconsistent copy data (:tickets:`#1359, #1360`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:119
msgid "Handle client encodings aliases (:ticket:`#1363`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:120
msgid "Fix building C extension with Cython 3.3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:124
msgid "Psycopg 3.3.4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:126
msgid ""
"Fix possible spurious connection timeout in systems with very long uptimes "
"in C extension (:ticket:`#1280`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:128
msgid ""
"Fix client-side adaptation of enums whose name require quotes "
"(:ticket:`#1298`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:130
msgid ""
"Consistently populate `~Cursor.statusmessage` after `~Cursor.executemany()` "
"(:ticket:`#1302`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:135
msgid "Psycopg 3.3.3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:137
msgid ""
"Retain `Error.pgconn` when raising a single exception for multiple "
"connection attempt errors (:ticket:`#1246`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:139
msgid ""
"Return a proper error when server sends ``ErrorResponse`` for a ``Sync`` "
"after a ``Parse`` (:ticket:`#1260`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:144
msgid "Psycopg 3.3.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:146
msgid "Fix race condition in adapters at startup (:ticket:`#1230`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:150
msgid "Psycopg 3.3.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:152
msgid "Fix iteration on server-side cursors (:ticket:`#1226`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:156
msgid "Psycopg 3.3.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:159 ../../../news.rst:379
msgid "New top-level features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:160
msgid ""
"Add :ref:`template strings queries <template-strings>` (:ticket:`#1054`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:161
msgid ""
"More flexible :ref:`composite adaptation<adapt-composite>`: it is now "
"possible to adapt Python objects to PostgreSQL composites and back even if "
"they are not sequences or if they take keyword arguments "
"(:ticket:`#932`, :ticket:`#1202`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:164
msgid ""
"Cursors are now iterators_, not just iterables_. This means you can call "
"`next`\\ ``(cur)`` or `anext`\\ ``(cur)``, which is useful as a :ref:`type-"
"safe expression <typing-fetchone>` (:ticket:`#1064`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:167
msgid ""
"Add `Cursor.set_result()` and `Cursor.results()` to move across the result "
"sets of queries executed though `~Cursor.executemany()` or "
"`~Cursor.execute()` with multiple statements (:tickets:`#1080, #1170`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:170
msgid ""
"Add :ref:`transaction-status` to report the status during and after a "
"`~Connection.transaction()` block (:ticket:`#969`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:172
msgid ""
"Allow to change loaders using `~adapt.AdaptersMap.register_loader()` on "
"`Cursor.adapters` after a query result has been already returned "
"(:ticket:`#884`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:177 ../../../news.rst:401
msgid "New libpq wrapper features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:178
msgid ""
"Add `pq.PGconn.used_gssapi` attribute and `Capabilities.has_used_gssapi()` "
"function (:ticket:`#1138`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:180
msgid ""
"Add `ConnectionInfo.full_protocol_version` attribute, "
"`Capabilities.has_full_protocol_version()` function (:ticket:`#1079`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:184 ../../../news.rst:412
msgid "Other changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:185
msgid ""
"Disable default GSSAPI preferential connection in the binary package "
"(:ticket:`#1136`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:190
msgid ""
"Please explicitly set the gssencmode_ connection parameter or "
"the :envvar:`PGGSSENCMODE` environment variable to interact reliably with "
"the GSSAPI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:194
msgid "Drop support for Python 3.8 (:ticket:`#976`) and 3.9 (:ticket:`#1056`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:201
msgid "Psycopg 3.2.13"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:203
msgid ""
"Show the host name in the error message in case of name resolution error "
"(:ticket:`#1205`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:205
msgid ""
"Fix `Cursor.copy()` and `AsyncCursor.copy()` to hold the connection lock for "
"the entire operation, preventing concurrent access issues (:ticket:`#1210`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:207
msgid ""
"Fix GSSAPI check with C extension built with libpq < v16 (:ticket:`#1216`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:211
msgid "Psycopg 3.2.12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:213
msgid ""
"Allow copy to pass different types per column, as long as the database can "
"convert them. Regression introduced in 3.2.11 (:ticket:`#1192`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:218
msgid "Psycopg 3.2.11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:220
msgid ""
"Fix spurious readiness flags in some of the wait functions (:ticket:`#1141`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:221
msgid ""
"Fix high CPU usage using the ``wait_c`` function on Windows (:ticket:`#645`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:222
msgid "Fix bad data on error in binary copy (:ticket:`#1147`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:223
msgid ""
"Respect `Copy.set_types()` in TEXT copy in C version, consistently with the "
"Python version (:ticket:`#1153`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:225
msgid ""
"Don't raise warning, and don't leak resources, if a builtin function is used "
"as JSON dumper/loader function (:ticket:`#1165`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:227
msgid ""
"Improve performance of Python conversion on results loading "
"(:ticket:`#1155`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:233
msgid "Psycopg 3.2.10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:235
msgid ""
"Fix `!TypeError` shadowing `~asyncio.CancelledError` upon task cancellation "
"during pipeline execution (:ticket:`#1005`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:237
msgid ""
"Fix memory leak when lambda/local functions are used as argument for "
"`~.psycopg.types.json.set_json_dumps()`, "
"`~.psycopg.types.json.set_json_loads()` (:ticket:`#1108`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:240
msgid ""
"Fix coordination of `~Cursor.executemany()` with other concurrent operations "
"on other cursors (:ticket:`#1130`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:242
msgid ""
"Fix leak receiving notifications if the `~Connection.notifies()` generator "
"is not called (:ticket:`#1091`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:247
msgid ""
"This bugfix required the introduction of a change in :ref:`notifies "
"reception <async-notify>` behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:250
msgid ""
"If a notification is received when a handler is registered via "
"`~Connection.add_notify_handler()` and the `~Connection.notifies()` "
"generator is not running the notification will not be yielded by the "
"generator. This is a behaviour similar to before `Psycopg 3.2.4`_, but "
"*notifications are not lost if no handler is registered*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:256
msgid ""
"Using both the generator and handlers to receive notifications on the same "
"connection is therefore deprecated and will now generate a runtime warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:260
msgid "Add support for Python 3.14 (:ticket:`#1053`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:261
msgid "Fix `psycopg_binary.__version__`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:262
msgid ""
"Raise a warning if a GSSAPI connection is obtained using the "
"``gssencmode=prefer`` libpq default (see :ticket:`#1136`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:267
msgid ""
"In a future Psycopg version the default in the binary package will be "
"changed to ``disable``. If you need to interact with the GSSAPI reliably you "
"should explicitly set the gssencmode_ parameter in the connection string or "
"the :envvar:`PGGSSENCMODE` environment variable to ``prefer`` or ``require``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:277
msgid "Psycopg 3.2.9"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:279
msgid ""
"Revert the libpq included in the binary packages from conda forge to vcpkg "
"because GSS connection crashes (:ticket:`#1088`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:284
msgid "Psycopg 3.2.8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:286
msgid ""
"Fix `DateFromTicks` and `TimeFromTicks` return values to return a date and a "
"time referred to the UTC timezone rather than to the local timezone. For "
"consistency, `TimestampFromTicks` to return a datetime in UTC rather than in "
"the local timezone (:ticket:`#1058`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:290
msgid ""
"Fix `~Cursor.rownumber` after using `~AsyncServerCursor.scroll()` on "
"`AsyncServerCursor` (:ticket:`#1066`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:292
msgid ""
"Fix interval parsing with days or other parts and negative time in C module "
"(:ticket:`#1071`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:294
msgid ""
"Don't process further connection attempts after Ctrl-C (:ticket:`#1077`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:295
msgid ""
"Fix cursors to correctly iterate over rows even if their row factory returns "
"`None` (:ticket:`#1073`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:297
msgid ""
"Fix `ConnectionInfo.port` when the port is specified as an empty string "
"(:ticket:`#1078`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:299
msgid ""
"Report all the attempts error messages in the exception raised for a "
"connection failure (:ticket:`#1069`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:301
msgid "Improve logging on connection (:ticket:`#1085`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:302
msgid "Add support for PostgreSQL 18 libpq (:ticket:`#1082`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:306
msgid "Psycopg 3.2.7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:308
msgid "Add SRID support to shapely dumpers/loaders (:ticket:`#1028`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:309
msgid "Add support for binary hstore (:ticket:`#1030`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:313
msgid "Psycopg 3.2.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:315
msgid ""
"Fix connection semantic when using ``target_session_attrs=prefer-standby`` "
"(:ticket:`#1021`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:320
msgid "Psycopg 3.2.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:322
msgid ""
"3x faster UUID loading thanks to C implementation (:tickets:`#447, #998`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:328
msgid "Psycopg 3.2.4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:330
msgid ""
"Don't lose notifies received whilst the `~Connection.notifies()` iterator is "
"not running (:ticket:`#962`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:335
msgid ""
"If you were using notifications to bridge the time between issuing a LISTEN "
"on a channel and starting the iterator you might receive duplicate "
"notifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:339
msgid ""
"Make sure that the notifies callback is called during the use of the "
"`~Connection.notifies()` generator (:ticket:`#972`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:341
msgid ""
"Raise the correct error returned by the database (such as `!AdminShutdown` "
"or `!IdleInTransactionSessionTimeout`) instead of a generic "
"`OperationalError` when a server error causes a client disconnection "
"(:ticket:`#988`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:345
msgid ""
"Build macOS dependencies from sources instead using the Homebrew versions in "
"order to avoid problems with ``MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET`` (:ticket:`#858`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:347
msgid "Bump libpq to 17.2 in Linux and macOS binary packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:348
msgid ""
"Bump libpq to 16.4 in Windows binary packages, using the `vcpkg library`__ "
"(:ticket:`#966`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:355
msgid "Psycopg 3.2.3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:357
msgid "Release binary packages including PostgreSQL 17 libpq (:ticket:`#852`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:361
msgid "Psycopg 3.2.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:363
msgid ""
"Drop `!TypeDef` specifications as string from public modules, as they cannot "
"be composed by users as `!typing` objects previously could (:ticket:`#860`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:365
msgid "Release Python 3.13 binary packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:369
msgid "Psycopg 3.2.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:371
msgid ""
"Fix packaging metadata breaking ``[c]``, ``[binary]`` dependencies "
"(:ticket:`#853`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:376
msgid "Psycopg 3.2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:380
msgid ""
"Add support for integer, floating point, boolean `NumPy scalar types`__ "
"(:ticket:`#332`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:382
msgid ""
"Add `!timeout` and `!stop_after` parameters to `Connection.notifies()` "
"(:ticket:`340`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:384
msgid ""
"Allow dumpers to return `!None`, to be converted to NULL (:ticket:`#377`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:385
msgid ""
"Add :ref:`raw-query-cursors` to execute queries using placeholders in "
"PostgreSQL format (`$1`, `$2`...) (:tickets:`#560, #839`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:387
msgid ""
"Add `capabilities` object to :ref:`inspect the libpq capabilities "
"<capabilities>` (:ticket:`#772`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:389
msgid ""
"Add `~rows.scalar_row` to return scalar values from a query (:ticket:`#723`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:390
msgid ""
"Add `~Connection.cancel_safe()` for encrypted and non-blocking cancellation "
"when using libpq v17. Use such method internally to implement `!"
"KeyboardInterrupt` and `~cursor.copy` termination (:ticket:`#754`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:393
msgid ""
"The `!context` parameter of `sql` objects `~sql.Composable.as_string()` and "
"`~sql.Composable.as_bytes()` methods is now optional (:ticket:`#716`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:395
msgid ""
"Add `~Connection.set_autocommit()` on sync connections, and similar "
"transaction control methods available on the async connections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:397
msgid ""
"Add a `size` parameter to `~Cursor.stream()` to enable results retrieval in "
"chunks instead of row-by-row (:ticket:`#794`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:402
msgid ""
"Add support for libpq functions to close prepared statements and portals "
"introduced in libpq v17 (:ticket:`#603`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:404
msgid ""
"Add support for libpq encrypted and non-blocking query cancellation "
"functions introduced in libpq v17 (:ticket:`#754`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:406
msgid ""
"Add support for libpq function to retrieve results in chunks introduced in "
"libpq v17 (:ticket:`#793`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:408
msgid ""
"Add support for libpq function to change role passwords introduced in libpq "
"v17 (:ticket:`#818`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:413
msgid "Drop support for Python 3.7."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:414
msgid ""
"Prepared statements are now :ref:`compatible with PgBouncer <pgbouncer>`. "
"(:ticket:`#589`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:416
msgid ""
"Disable receiving more than one result on the same cursor in pipeline mode, "
"to iterate through `~Cursor.nextset()`. The behaviour was different than in "
"non-pipeline mode and not totally reliable (:ticket:`#604`). The `Cursor` "
"now only preserves the results set of the last `~Cursor.execute()`, "
"consistently with non-pipeline mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:426
msgid "Psycopg 3.1.20"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:428
msgid ""
"Use the simple query protocol to execute COMMIT/ROLLBACK when possible. This "
"should make querying the PgBouncer admin database easier (:ticket:`#820`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:431
msgid ""
"Avoid unneeded escaping checks and memory over-allocation in text copy "
"(:ticket:`#829`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:433
msgid "Bundle binary package with OpenSSL 3.3.x (:ticket:`#847`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:434
msgid ""
"Drop macOS ARM64 binary packages for macOS versions before 14.0 and Python "
"before 3.10 (not for our choice but for the lack of available CI "
"runners; :ticket:`#858`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:440
msgid "Psycopg 3.1.19"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:442
msgid ""
"Fix unaligned access undefined behaviour in C extension (:ticket:`#734`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:443
msgid "Fix excessive stripping of error message prefixes (:ticket:`#752`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:444
msgid ""
"Allow to specify the ``connect_timeout`` connection parameter as float "
"(:ticket:`#796`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:446
msgid "Improve COPY performance on macOS (:ticket:`#745`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:450
msgid "Psycopg 3.1.18"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news.rst:452
